Properties with free-form text -- such as ``summary``, ``description``, ``location``, ``comments``, and ``contacts`` -- now return their value normalized to Unicode NFC, so values that differ only in how a diacritic was encoded (NFC vs NFD) compare and display consistently. Normalization happens when the value is read, not when the file is parsed, so ``to_ical()`` still round-trips the original bytes unchanged. ``CATEGORIES`` is the one exception: its items are normalized when the list is built, so re-serializing a file with NFD categories now writes NFC. Identifier-like properties such as ``UID``, ``PRODID``, and ``URL`` are left untouched. @HannaEpelboim @GabrielGervasio @Mrbozz